      "content": "it's not about \"evading\" something illegal, i'm just worried about my privacy at work. if the chair is picking up my stress levels or my heart rate, that's huge personal data being collected without my consent. i just want to know how to sit so that my vitals stay as steady and \"neutral\" as possible so they don't get an inaccurate reading of my mood or focus. like, are there specific ways to breathe or use posture to keep my heart rate from spiking if i'm feeling frustrated? i just want to protect my own data.",
